ID cards are also attendance cards — the number on the card is the **RFID** on the person's record,
which is what makes their scans register. So a lost card is an attendance problem, not just an
identity one.

There are two screens. **Administration → ID Cards** manages the blank card pool, designs and lost-card
replacement. **Students → Student ID Cards** records where each student's card is in its life. They
need separate access.

**You need:** access to **Administration → ID Cards** for the first part, and to Student ID Cards for
[Tracking student cards](#tracking-student-cards).

## The blank card pool

The pool is the stock of unissued cards. Add cards to it as you receive them from your supplier; the
screen tells you what is left. Issuing draws from this pool, so an empty pool is why issuing fails.

## Card designs

Under **Card designs**, upload your institute's design as a PDF — separately for **Student card**
and **Teacher card**. This is held for reference, so whoever prints has the right artwork; the
printed card itself is produced from it.

**Upload PDF** adds one, **Replace** swaps it, and removal is immediate (**Card design removed**).

## Replacing a lost card

1. Open **Administration → ID Cards** and choose **Report a lost card**.
2. Pick **Student** or **Teacher**.
3. Enter the **Student ID** or **Teacher ID**.
4. Select **Issue Temporary Card**.
5. **Print** the card.

The temporary card carries a new number, and that number becomes the person's active RFID. Their old
card stops working — which is the point, since it is presumably in someone else's hands.

## If someone's attendance stops working

Check their card before anything else. The two usual causes are a lost card that was never reported,
so scans are going to a dead number, and a record that never had an RFID filled in at all — see
[Add a Student](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-student).

## Tracking student cards

**Students → Student ID Cards** keeps a record of every student's card: whether it has been printed,
whether it has been handed over, and what happened if it was lost or damaged. Changing a card's status
needs the separate manage permission; without it the list is read-only.

### The list

Every student appears with their **Name**, **Student ID**, **Class**, **RFID**, **Status**, **Reason**
and **Updated** date. Column headers sort. Use the filters to narrow it:

- **Search name, student ID or RFID**
- **Class** (*All classes* by default)
- **Status**, showing how many students are in each state; **Reset** clears the filters.

The statuses are **Not printed**, **Printed**, **Distributed**, **Lost**, **Damaged**, **Returned**,
**Replaced** and **Other**. A student with no card recorded yet shows as *Not printed*.

The export menu on the page downloads the filtered list, including the Printed and Handed over dates
and the reason a card has not been printed.

### Why a card isn't printed

If a student's card is still *Not printed* and their record is incomplete, the **Reason** column shows
in red, for example *Missing photo, address*. A card needs the student's **photo**, **address** and
**phone number** on file. Open the student's profile, add what is missing, and the reason clears. A
blank, *N/A* or absent value counts as missing.

### Mark cards printed or handed over

1. Tick the students you want, or tick the header to select the whole filtered list.
2. Use **Mark printed** or **Mark distributed**; the button shows how many are selected, for example
   *Mark printed (12)*. Both buttons are at the top of the page.

For one student, use the menu on their row (**Change status**) to pick any status. A note is
required for **Other** (*Add a note saying what happened.*) and optional for the rest. When the
status is **Lost** or **Damaged** you can also choose **Start a replacement card**, which adds a new
*Not printed* card to the list.

### Quick add at the handover desk

**Quick add** is for handing out cards one after another:

1. Select **Quick add**.
2. Type or scan the **Student ID** and the card's **RFID**, then **Verify**.
3. Check the student shown. The screen warns you if the card is already linked to this student, if it
   will replace their current card, or if the RFID cannot be used because another record holds it.
4. **Confirm** records the card as linked and handed over.

Cards added this way are listed under **Added this session**.

### On the student's profile

A student's profile has an **ID Card** section showing the card number (RFID), when it was printed
and handed over, any note, and a **History** of every change. **Update** there changes the status
the same way as the list does.

